      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. but it needs to be a bit more formal and strict. like, i should probably mention that i am aware of my rights regarding heating in germany and that if it isnt fixed soon i might have to look into reducing the rent (Mietminderung). can you rewrite it to be more assertive and include a deadline for the repair? maybe say they have 5 days to respond?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Subject: Urgent: Mandatory Radiator Repair and Potential Financial Adjustment\n\nDear Hoheitsvter [Landlord’s Name],\n\nI am writing to you concerning the malfunctioning radiator in my living room. As I am completely aware of my statutory entitlements concerning adequate heating in Germany, I would like to remind you that this issue must be resolved expeditiously to ensure conformity with the agreed rent's implied warranty of habitability. I must emphasize that I reserve the right to claim for Mietminderung (rent reduction) if this maintenance work is not undertaken immediately.\n\nPer Article 555 ff. of the German Civil Code (Bürgerliches Gesetzbuch), I have every legal right to request lived in premises that cannot be used to its full rental potential without the necessary heating, due to expected interior temperatures in the colder seasons. This is not merely a suggestion, but a formal demand for an urgent assessment, followed by timely repairs and a full report on the assessed need for Mietminderung.\n\nPlease be advised that failure to maintain the radiators will result in subsequent action on my part, including appropriately formal claims for rent reduction. I expect your response by this Friday. This is a non-negotiable deadline, and I trust your swift attention to the matter",
      "source": "target",
